# Episode work folders hold the heavy intermediates: source footage, ProRes alpha
# layers, PNG frame sequences, TTS audio and the rendered master. All of that is
# reproducible from the small files we DO track (episode.json, the script, the
# plan, the fetched Steam facts) plus the scripts in scripts/pipeline + scripts/motion.
#
# Ignore everything inside an episode folder, then whitelist the source of truth.
*/*
!*/episode.json
!*/script.json
!*/script_timed.json
!*/plan.json
!*/plan_short.json
!*/desc.txt
!*/facts.json
# teardown.md carries the evidence AND the shell commands that regenerate every
# ignored asset (evidence cards, spec layers, thumbnail) plus the trailer windows
# that are safe to cut from. Without it a fresh clone has the scripts but not the
# arguments, and the episode is not actually reproducible. Every episode needs one.
!*/teardown.md
# Korean side-by-side of the narration, so the user can review an English episode
!*/script_ko.md
# Exact caption track — a real search signal, and tiny
!*/captions.*.srt
!*/analysis.md
!*/analysis_ko.md
!*/thumb.jpg
!*/still_bg.png
!*/README.md
!*/reviews.json
# reviews_all.json is the 800-review corpus analyze_reviews.py builds; it is the
# evidence behind the claims in teardown.md, so it is worth the ~1 MB.
!*/reviews_all.json
!*/appdetails_*.json
!*/short.json
!*/short_timed.json
!*/episode_short.json
!*/desc_short.txt
# 9:16 thumbnail for the Short (make_thumbnail.py --vertical)
!*/thumb_short.jpg
# caption-form script -> spoken-form (pron_*.json); the *_tts_timed file is what build_plan reads
!*/script_tts.json
!*/script_tts_timed.json
!*/short_tts.json
!*/short_tts_timed.json
